# Selected recovery and actual metadata scope

The complete new author derivation and report, top-level textual metadata/search streams, freeze and actual completion receipt are captured exactly. Current already-read instruction sources are copied. All34 author frozen members, including the PDF and historical recovery bodies, are verified at their original paths. PDF and old recovery bodies are not recursively copied or claimed semantically read. Historical parent manifests do not become theorem dependencies or a promise of a recursively complete archive.

The author's self-recorded metadata capture/finalization receipts are preserved with their original scope. They are not upgraded into missing subprocess source-at-launch/streams or into scientific runs. The original literature web read was not contemporaneously archived; a later PDF retrieval does not change that limitation. The new review has its own actual bounded metadata subprocess receipts with source-at-launch, UTC start/end, stdout, stderr, failures, timeout and exit code.

The final freeze covers every nested file actually present here by full path, excluding only its own exact root path. Original candidate files, historical packets, W and Git remain unchanged. Source-current matches are recorded mechanically and kept separate from complete reading coverage and mathematical judgment.
